rfc768.txt, rfc2675.txt, rfc6335.txt, rfc6935.txt, rfc6936.txt, rfc8085.txt
    The texts of RFC 768 (User Datagram Protocol), RFC 2675 (IPv6 Jumbograms), RFC 6335 (the procedures
    of the Service Name and Transport Protocol Port Number Registry), RFC 6935 (IPv6 and UDP Checksums
    for Tunneled Packets), RFC 6936 (Applicability Statement for the Use of IPv6 UDP Datagrams with Zero
    Checksums) and RFC 8085 (UDP Usage Guidelines), downloaded from https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/ on
    2026-10-27.
    License: the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents.
    Used: the header format, the checksum and its zero value, the length of jumbograms, and the
    requirements of the zero checksum of IPv6 that the tests check.

linux.txt
    Frames that the Linux kernel (7.0.14-linuxkit, of Docker Desktop on arm64, with the tools of Debian
    trixie) sent between two network namespaces on 2026-10-27: UDP echoes over IPv4 and IPv6 (Python
    echo servers), an empty and an odd-length payload, an IPv4 datagram without a checksum
    (SO_NO_CHECK), an IPv6 datagram with a zero checksum (UDP_NO_CHECK6_TX, to a socket with
    UDP_NO_CHECK6_RX, RFC 6935), datagrams of 3,072 bytes fragmented by the sender over a link of an MTU
    of 1,500, and datagrams to a closed port with the Port Unreachable errors they caused. Two MLDv2
    reports of the start are kept. Checksum offloading was turned off.
    Each frame is a line of hexadecimal after "# " lines with tcpdump's summary of it (`tcpdump -n -e -v`).
    Made by linux.sh, run as `docker run --rm --privileged -v "$PWD":/out debian:trixie sh /out/linux.sh`,
    and `python3 ../ethernet/linux.py udp.pcap udp.txt linux.txt`.
    License: produced for this project (no third-party content).
